<title>USA: Salomon to offer funds in Brazil.</title>
<headline>Salomon to offer funds in Brazil.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Salomon Brothers Asset Management Inc and its Brazilian affiliate, Banco Patrimonio, formed an alliance with Banco Bradesco to offer a new group of mutual funds to Brazilian investors, Salomon said.</p>
<p>Salomon said they will offer three portfolios: conservative, or short and medium-term investments; moderate, or medium-term investments; and aggressive, or long-term investments.</p>
<p>The funds will be allocated among equities, bank certificates of deposit, fixed-income securities, dollar-denominated commercial paper, and foreign debt.</p>
<p>Salomon Asset Management is a unit of Salomon Inc.</p>
